*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
.env
.venv/
venv/

# Node
node_modules/
chirp-server/frontend/dist/

# Data (never commit user data or secrets)
chirp-server/data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.wav
*.opus
*.flac
*.mp3
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
!chirp-logo.svg
# Real documentation screenshots (README.md's own Screenshots section)
# are meant to be committed, unlike the blanket rule above (which
# exists to stop runtime-downloaded bird photos and real user data from
# ever being committed, not to catch intentional docs). A real bug
# found from actual GitHub usage, not a hypothetical: these files exist
# in every local checkout of this repo, but the blanket *.jpg/*.png
# rule above silently excluded them from every `git add`, so they were
# never actually committed or pushed — the README's own <img> tags
# point to files that genuinely don't exist in the real GitHub repo,
# rendering as broken images there even though they render fine
# locally (a person's own local file browser or editor doesn't care
# whether something is git-tracked, so this was invisible outside of
# actually checking GitHub itself).
!docs/screenshots/**
# Same real bug, same fix, recurring: figures/ (renamed from
# patent_figures/) and every techdocs assets/ copy (the standalone
# MkDocs site's own copy, plus each server's bundled copy for the
# in-app admin Tech Docs page — see scripts/sync-techdocs.py) hit this
# exact blanket rule too. Confirmed directly: README.md's embedded
# <img> tags for the system architecture / detection pipeline figures
# rendered as broken images on GitHub for the same reason
# docs/screenshots did above, before these exceptions existed.
!figures/**
!techdocs/docs/assets/**
!chirp-server/app/techdocs_content/assets/**
!chirp-server-instances/app/techdocs_content/assets/**
*.gpkg

# Docker
.docker/

